Traffic Watch — third-party data and services
=============================================

The Traffic Watch code is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It displays data from the
services and datasets below, each under its own terms. Data marked "bundled"
ships in data/ref/; everything else is fetched at runtime on your machine.

Bundled reference data (data/ref/)
----------------------------------
- roads.json — highways from Natural Earth (public domain,
  https://www.naturalearthdata.com) and, for Alaska, Hawaii and Japan,
  OpenStreetMap. Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the
  Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
- places.json, ports.json — Natural Earth (public domain).
- airports.json — OurAirports (public domain, https://ourairports.com/data/).
- airlines.json — derived from OpenFlights airlines.dat, Open Database License
  (ODbL) 1.0, https://openflights.org/data.html, with additions.
- mid.json — derived from powers9/MIDs, Apache License 2.0,
  https://github.com/powers9/MIDs
- types.json — ICAO Doc 8643 aircraft type designators, as published by the
  OpenSky Network (https://opensky-network.org).

Downloaded on first run (not redistributed)
-------------------------------------------
- aircraft.sqlite — built from tar1090-db (https://github.com/wiedehopf/tar1090-db).

Live services (your own access, under each service's terms)
-----------------------------------------------------------
- OpenSky Network — aircraft positions. Matthias Schäfer, Martin Strohmeier,
  Vincent Lenders, Ivan Martinovic and Matthias Wilhelm. "Bringing Up OpenSky:
  A Large-scale ADS-B Sensor Network for Research". IPSN 2014.
  Terms: https://opensky-network.org/about/terms-of-use (non-commercial use).
- AISStream.io — ship positions (https://aisstream.io).
- aviationweather.gov (NOAA/NWS Aviation Weather Center) — METAR, TAF, PIREP.
- api.weather.gov (US National Weather Service) — US daily forecasts.
- Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com) — forecasts outside the US, CC BY 4.0.
- RainViewer (https://www.rainviewer.com) — radar outside the mainland US.
- Iowa Environmental Mesonet — NEXRAD radar tiles (mainland US).
- Esri — gray canvas base map tiles (Esri, HERE, Garmin, © OpenStreetMap contributors).
- Chart.js (MIT), Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause) and folium (MIT) power the map and charts.

Ship operators shown in the app are inferred from ship names and may be wrong.
Aircraft owners are hidden for aircraft in the FAA LADD/PIA privacy programmes.
